Affected module/version: cumm 0.5.3, cu130-rev1 amd64 SDK (TensorView headers).
Observed failure: Clang 21 instantiates std::copy for forbidden integer/half and
half/bfloat conversions while forming the callback passed to if_constexpr,
even though is_convertible rejects the conversion and that branch is discarded.
Rationale/scope: use C++17 if constexpr in astype so invalid copy expressions are
actually discarded. Preserve conversion dispatch, allowed dtype pairs and the
SDK binary ABI. Consumers must use C++17 or newer; no library payload is changed.
Verification: Clang 21.1.8/GNU 13.3.0, CUDA 13.2.2, x86_64: @spconv//:abi_test
passes real container/allocator ownership, GPU sorting, float/half round trips
and rejected int64/half conversion. All 18 original autoware_tensorrt_plugins
cases and both added libc++/TensorRT loading and serialized-engine cases pass.
Upstream status: checked 2026-11-19, FindDefinition/cumm main
 d971d02a0b29b7e6da46186564f37bde77b99dcc still uses callback dispatch.
No matching fix associated or submission made. Related reports (not matching
fixes): https://github.com/FindDefinition/cumm/issues/23 and
https://github.com/traveller59/spconv/issues/658.

